    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d787">

                <pb facs="0893" n="1727" xml:id="pg1727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/11575</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-28T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1918, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received September 29, 10.12 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1875. Embassy’s 1864, September 23, 7 p.m. Minister for Foreign Affairs stated
                    yesterday to Portuguese Minister for Foreign Affairs that Spanish Government
                    would hardly take action concerning seizure of German boat or boats before
                    reassembling of Cortes probably October 15. Nevertheless it is general belief of
                    Allied diplomats here, in which Embassy concurs, that such seizure will be made
                    only after secret ultimatum [<hi rendition="#italic">understanding
                    between?</hi>] Spanish Government and German Ambassador. However, if they are
                    accepted [<hi rendition="#italic">continued?</hi>], Allied successes may
                    influence Spain to more positive stand toward Germany, although it is thought
                    latter is constantly holding out inducement to Spain that she will be called
                    upon to intervene between belligerents.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
